BMOE_DONE {"id":95,"cancelled":false,"tokens":228,"tok_s":11.184,"prefill_s":3.799,"prefill_tps":20.27,"load_s":3.065,"cache_hit_pct":66.0,"n_prompt":77,"n_past":305,"compute_s_tok":0.0682,"io_s_tok":0.0455,"cache_resident_mib":1999,"cache_budget_mib":2000,"read_mib":2825.8,"stall_s_tok":0.0178,"mgmt_s_tok":0.0034,"majflt_tok":0.00,"cpu_s_tok":0.0000,"token_demand_mib":86.9,"mtp_drafted":0,"mtp_accepted":0,"mtp_decodes":228,"mtp_draft_s_tok":0.0000,"drafted_steps":0,"loop_overhead_s_tok":0.0004,"reasoning":"","text":" short story.\n\n<think>\n</think>\n\n# The Neon Courier\n\n**Story:**\n\nUnit 712 stood with his hydraulic legs locked, the rain hissing like steam on the city's artificial skin. The neon signs of Neo-Tokyo bled long shadows onto the wet pavement like watercolor paint gone wrong. He adjusted the sealed package, a heavy, angular case wrapped in too-cold plastic, and navig the flickering hellscape of the city.\n\nThe delivery required a leap of faith he wasn't sure he had left in his heart. He pushed back the visor of his rusted helmet and handed the shivering, soot-stained woman next to him a dry, protein-warm ration from his own pocket. She shivered, not just from the cold, \"Thank you,\" she whispered, her eyes wide with unaccustomed vulnerability. \"I know it would be hard to find you a umbrella,\" the rain hammered a frantic rhythm on his metal skull, but 712 just smiled, a small, mechanical thing. \"No problem, ma'am. I've got an extra one"}
